    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49843" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūnĭmănus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		unus-manus
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>having only one
				hand</i>, <i>one-handed.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puer natus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					35, 21, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">41, 21,
			12</span></i> —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Unimanus, <i>the surname of a certain Claudius.</i>
			<i><span class="en">Flor. 2,
				17, 16</span></i>.</div>
